# Keep the build context small and the image clean. Everything here is either
# rebuilt inside the Dockerfile, machine-local, or a secret.

# Rust build output — gigabytes, and a host-built target/ is the wrong
# architecture for the image anyway. bin/ is the Replit build's staged binary.
target/
**/target/
bin/
**/*.rs.bk

# Node modules are reinstalled from the committed lockfile via `npm ci`.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# The SPA is rebuilt in the frontend stage. A stale host dist/ must never be
# copied in — it would silently ship whatever was last built on a laptop.
dist/
**/dist/
.vite/
**/.vite/

# SQLite lives on the /data volume, never in the image. The local database
# sits at backend/mena_ai.db, so these need the `**/` prefix — a bare `*.db`
# only matches at the context root.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.db.snapshot
**/*.db.restore
**/*.db.gz
**/*.sqlite.gz

# Secrets. Tokens reach the container through compose's env_file at runtime,
# never through the image. Real files exist at the repo root and in backend/,
# so this needs `**/` — a bare `.env` matches only the context root.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Git, CI and deployment metadata are not needed to build.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
Caddyfile
.replit
.replitignore
replit.nix

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Docs — not needed at build or runtime. methodology/ is NOT listed: the
# backend compiles those documents into the binary.
README.md
LICENSE
